  "results": [
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_1",
      "question": "What are the wizards asking the council to do in the emergency meeting-and what's the catch?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "semantic_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "tradeoff"
      ],
      "semantic_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "tradeoff"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 0.5,
      "failure_surface": "synthesis_gap",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "wizards' college": "synthesis_gap",
        "arcane lockdown": "hit",
        "wards": "synthesis_gap",
        "tradeoff": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The wizards are pushing for a **citywide arcane lockdown**, but the catch is it could **isolate parts of the city and impact the entire population**, risking economic disruption and trapping people inside problem zones.\n\nFrom the projection:\n\n- **CANON / OBSERVED alignment:** The city has a **\u201cProposed arcane lockdown\u201d** (CANON) and a **\u201cPlanned magical lockdown\u201d** (OBSERVED), indicating this is the central plan being debated in the emergency meeting.\n- The intent is to secure the city\u2019s **failing defenses** and counter the cult operating through **hidden routes and infrastructure**.\n\n**The catch:**\n- **OBSERVED:** The city is \u201cat risk of having parts isolated if key tunnels or access points are sealed.\u201d\n- **CANON/OBSERVED context:** The plan affects the **entire city population** and threatens a **festival-critical economy**, meaning large-scale disruption.\n- This creates a tradeoff: \u0938\u0941\u0930\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093e vs. mobility, safety vs. economic stability.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Proposed arcane lockdown; concerns about integrity\n- Geography: Hidden passages, sewers, citywide purification scope\n- Economy: Festival-dependent, major trade hub\n- Operational Status: Planned lockdown; city under threat from cult\n- Governance: Council actively choosing response to crisis",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_session_12_council_chamber_roster",
