        "guards": "hit",
        "ephanna": "synthesis_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The fight in the council chamber involves the Players, the Wolf, Thalia, and multiple Guards (including elite units); no explicit confirmation of council members being present during the fight.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Participants (OBSERVED/CANON):\n  - Players: Present and actively engaged; \u201cParty is actively in battle and initially effective.\u201d\n  - the Wolf: Central adversary in the council chamber battle; uses illusions and attempts escape.\n  - Thalia (Commander of the Guard): Present with the Wolf (\u201cWolf is standing at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d) and fights after his instruction.\n  - Guards: Present in force; includes \u201c8 regular guards (half corrupted) and 2 elite guards,\u201d with activity around/near the Council Chambers and direct combat involvement.\n\n- Combat Context:\n  - Guards are \u201cactively stopping people outside Council Chambers\u201d and engaging \u0627\u0644\u062f\u0627\u062e\u0644.\n  - Elite guards directly attack party members.\n  - The Wolf is both fighting and attempting escape (including invisibility and secret passage).\n\n- Not Confirmed:\n  - No explicit statement that council members remain in the chamber during the fight.\n\nIf you need exact staging (positions, waves, or who starts where), the projection doesn\u2019t specify further.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_campaign_general_notes_1",
      "question": "Who are the Shepherds, and what god or power do they answer to?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
