        "counter corruption": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright represents the wizards, and he takes a hardline, proactive stance\u2014treating the cult as a dire magical threat and pushing for detection magic and a citywide arcane lockdown.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (OBSERVED/CANON) is the Head of the Wizard\u2019s College and serves as the council\u2019s arcane representative.  \n\nHis angle on the cult is aggressive and solution-driven:\n- He views the corrupted meat as \u201ca perversion of magic\u201d (CANON) and takes the threat extremely seriously.\n- He is eager to deploy the Wizard\u2019s College\u2019s resources to detect and counteract the cult\u2019s influence (OBSERVED).\n- His concrete proposals include using a rune to locate corrupted meat and implementing a magical lockdown of the city (OBSERVED).\n- He is positioned to present his plan first, indicating a leading role in shaping the council\u2019s response (OBSERVED).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; arcane representative on the council  \n- Goals: Magical lockdown, detection runes, active countermeasures against the cult  \n- Attitude toward cult: Sees it as dangerous, corrupt magic requiring decisive intervention  \n- Approach: Systematic, magical surveillance and containment rather than political or social measures",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
