      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight **dead \u2014 \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** This overrides earlier escape/invisibility beats.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**:\n- He **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and was **\u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible\u201d** (escape trajectory).\n- But also **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (terminal outcome).\n\nPer the terminal outcome rule, the decapitation is the final, current state. That means any prior escape attempt did not ultimately succeed or was interrupted\u2014he does not get away.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: central adversary in the council chamber fight\n- Operational Status: previously escaping while invisible (overridden)\n- Physical Condition: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\n- Tactics (CANON): uses illusory duplicates to confuse pursuit\n\nNet: the fight resolves with the Wolf killed in the chamber, not fled.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
