      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence in the projection that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; her behavior is tied to The Wolf\u2019s direct influence (\u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d), which suggests something different or at least unconfirmed.\n\nFrom what\u2019s **OBSERVED**, the guards\u2019 corruption is clearly marked by \u201can oily sheen to their eyes\u201d and links to cult influence. Thalia, however, is only described in relation to The Wolf\u2014specifically, he \u201corders Thalia to attack the group,\u201d and is even \u201cstanding at Thalia\u2019s shoulder.\u201d There\u2019s no mention of her showing the guards\u2019 corruption signs (like oily eyes) or interacting with corrupted meat mechanics.\n\nSo based strictly on the projection:\n- Guards = explicitly corrupted (visible signs, mechanical effects).\n- Thalia = acting under The Wolf\u2019s direction, but **no confirmed corruption markers**.\n\nThat makes her situation either different (e.g., manipulation, coercion, or another effect) or simply not yet revealed.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Corruption markers (Guards): \u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Thalia behavior: \u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d (OBSERVED, via The Wolf)\n- The Wolf: \u201ccorrupting_influence\u201d tag; manipulative, deceptive, cult-aligned (CANON/OBSERVED)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_2",
      "question": "What does the council room itself throw at us that screws with the fight?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "semantic_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "must_hits": [
        "arcane traps",
