        "guard operations": "synthesis_gap",
        "uncertain reliability": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia is compromised or under influence\u2014do not trust her in the meeting.\n\nThere\u2019s no direct profile for Thalia, but **OBSERVED facts about the Wolf** strongly implicate her situation. The Wolf is:\n- **\u201cstanding at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d** (OBSERVED)\n- Actively attempting deception and manipulation in the council\n- Explicitly **\u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d** (OBSERVED)\n\nThe Wolf is also a **cultist saboteur** working to mislead the council and undermine decisions, with a pattern of deception and influence. Additionally, the presence of **corruption indicators (e.g., oily sheen in eyes affecting others like guards)** suggests a broader mind- or body-altering influence in play.\n\nGiven that proximity plus direct command influence, Thalia is very likely being controlled, coerced, or manipulated in real time.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Wolf proximity: \u201cstanding at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Wolf intent: deception, sabotage, misdirection (OBSERVED/CANON)\n- Direct influence: \u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Faction threat: cultist infiltration of leadership (OBSERVED)\n\nConclusion: Something is definitely off\u2014treat Thalia as compromised until proven otherwise.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_4_v2",
      "question": "If the council keeps talking and doesn't act, what bites us?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
