      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The cult advances unchecked\u2014moving through hidden routes, exploiting weak defenses, and pushing their summoning\u2014while the city drifts closer to disaster with each delayed decision.\n\nIf the council stalls, the biggest bite is **momentum loss against the cult**. CANON and OBSERVED both support that **the cult is already active below the city, using hidden infrastructure and alternative routes**, and aims to **access the heart of the city and complete a summoning (flesh kaiju)**. Delay gives them time to **bypass blocked routes, corrupt cauldrons, and continue coordinated actions**.\n\nAt the same time, OBSERVED city status is explicit: **the city is \u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate.\u201d** A proposed **arcane lockdown** exists (CANON), but inaction risks it never being implemented\u2014or being too late\u2014while **less fortified areas** remain vulnerable.\n\nThere\u2019s also internal risk: CANON notes **cult influence in the council**, so more talking increases chances of **misdirection or sabotage from within**.\n\nFinally, stakes escalate economically and socially: the **festival (key to the economy)** and **public unrest over tolls** create a volatile backdrop the cult can exploit.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Weak points; proposed arcane lockdown (not enacted)\n- Operational Status: Disaster risk increases with delay\n- Threat: Cult using hidden routes; summoning objective\n- Governance: Council infiltrated/influenced; indecision ongoing\n- Economy: Festival-critical; disruption likely if crisis escalates",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
