      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room is tense and visibly disrupted\u2014illusion traces fading, guards shaken (some corrupted), and the Wolf\u2019s body showing clear signs of the fight and corruption, including **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d** and oily eyes.\n\nAfter the fight, you should notice a mix of physical aftermath and eerie signals of the deeper threat:\n\n- The Wolf: His body is unmistakably finished\u2014**\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d**\u2014and **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d** marks the corruption behind his actions (OBSERVED).\n- Illusion residue: The Wolf used illusory duplicates (CANON), so the room may still feel visually \u201coff\u201d\u2014players were previously disoriented by illusion effects (CANON), suggesting lingering confusion or fading magical distortions.\n- Guards: Positioned around the chamber (OBSERVED), they appear **visibly tense** and some show **oily sheen in their eyes** (OBSERVED), signaling ongoing corruption within their ranks.\n- Arcane environment: Rune alarms and traps were active nearby (OBSERVED), and the city\u2019s ever-present **low hum of embedded mechanisms** (CANON) may shift subtly, especially after the conflict.\n- Structural/space cues: The chamber connects to **hidden passages beneath it** (CANON), reinforcing that something larger is operating below the surface.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps, rune alarms (OBSERVED/CANON)\n- Inhabitants: Guards (some corrupted), council presence implied\n- Notable Features: Hidden passage access beneath chamber (CANON)\n- Atmosphere: Tense, unstable, with lingering illusion effects and corruption signs",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
