      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room was heavily disrupted\u2014**almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball**, its magical defenses activated, and the space left **disheveled** with illusions and wards altering the environment.\n\nDuring Session 12 (OBSERVED):\n- A major destructive event occurred: **almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball**, implying widespread scorching or blast damage across the chamber.\n- The room\u2019s defenses reacted: **runes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell**, changing how the space functioned mid-encounter.\n- Illusory effects became active or relevant: **Illusory Walls are present in portions of the room**, affecting movement and perception.\n- Overall condition shifted to **Disheveled**, indicating physical disruption (furniture, table, or layout likely disturbed, though not itemized).\n\nThese changes override the room\u2019s typical pristine, ceremonial state (CANON), reflecting active combat and magical interference.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Atmosphere: \u201calmost the entire room is lit up by Fireball\u201d\n- Defenses: Activated runes; Illusory Walls; magical wards engaged\n- Physical Condition: Disheveled\n- Geography: Large circular chamber with central table (likely impacted but not explicitly destroyed)",
