      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead \u2014 **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** \u2014 so whatever corruption he had is no longer active in play.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**; previously had \u201can oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d\n- Operational Status (OBSERVED): Earlier escaped while invisible and attempted to flee via secret passage.\n- Mental State (OBSERVED): Desperate, regretful, even begging to be killed.\n- Faction/Alignment (OBSERVED): Cultist; betrayed Mirathorn.\n\nResolution of Conflicts:\nThere\u2019s a clear progression conflict between escape (invisible, fleeing) and death. The **terminal outcome \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** overrides earlier escape states, as it represents the final observed condition at end of session. Supporting this, **ent_bonogo** is noted to have \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d\n\nConclusion:\nAt the end of Session 12, the Wolf is definitively dead. His prior corruption (e.g., oily eyes) is no longer functionally relevant unless you introduce post-mortem effects or resurrection.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
