      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events and trying to escape; after, he is **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, ending his agency entirely.\n\n**Before the council fight (OBSERVED + CANON):**\n- **Role/Status:** Second-in-command of the guard; active cult-aligned saboteur influencing the council.\n- **Tactics:** Uses **illusory duplicates** (CANON) and deception to confuse players and mislead discussions.\n- **Behavior:** Orders attacks (e.g., Thalia), attempts to steer council decisions, and **drinks an invisibility potion to escape via a secret tunnel**.\n- **Mental State:** Alert, deceptive, but also shows cracks\u2014**desperate, begging for release or death, regretful**.\n- **Condition:** Mobile, dangerous; noted **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d** indicating corruption.\n\n**After the council fight (OBSERVED):**\n- **Physical Condition:** **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n- **Operational Status:** No longer active; escape and manipulation efforts are over.\n- **Threat Level:** Neutralized as a direct actor (though prior schemes may persist).\n\n**Key Attributes:**\n- Rank/Title: second-in-command of the guard  \n- Defenses: illusory duplicates  \n- Goals: deception, escape, sabotage  \n- Mental State: desperate, regretful  \n- Physical Condition: **Decapitated; head removed from body**; oily sheen in eyes",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_thalia",
      "question": "Was Thalia corrupted or just played-and how does that tie to the Wolf?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
