      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **not corrupted**\u2014she was **ensorcelled/controlled by the Wolf**, meaning she was being played rather than willingly turned.\n\nThalia\u2019s state is clearly different from true corruption. She **\u201cdoes not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED), while that oily sheen is consistently associated with corruption in guards and the Wolf\u2019s influence. Instead, she is explicitly **\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d** and even **\u201censorcelled (unbeknownst to her)\u201d** (OBSERVED), which aligns with mind control or magical coercion\u2014not conversion.\n\nHer behavior supports this: she **attacks the group after the Wolf's instruction** and **serves the Wolf**, but is also described as **innocent**, **defensive of her guard**, and later **realizes how dire the situation truly is** once her **charmed status ended** (OBSERVED). That shift strongly indicates her agency returns once the influence breaks.\n\nThe Wolf\u2019s role ties directly in: he is a **corrupting influence** (CANON) who **orders Thalia to attack the group** (OBSERVED) and specializes in deception and manipulation.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia physical_condition: ensorcelled; no oily sheen (OBSERVED)\n- Thalia mental_state: innocent; charmed status ended; realization afterward (OBSERVED)\n- Thalia loyalty: serves the Wolf (under influence) (OBSERVED)\n- Wolf role: corrupting influence; manipulator; gives commands (CANON/OBSERVED)\n\nConclusion: Thalia was being used as a puppet by the Wolf, not genuinely corrupted.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
  ],
